## Thesis reading

### What is the thesis about?

Chelsea Finn's thesis, "Learning to learn with gradients" is about solving meta learning with deep learning methods (gradient learning with large dataset).
She introduce the classic problem of meta-learning using pre-training and post-training principle that is widely used in deep learning researchs.
We can see pre-training as phase training with huge amounts of dataset so that the model can generalize to other task settings and post-training as learning phase shich quickly adapt to the new scenarios.

From the introduction I could see her researches being,

1. definition of meta-learning
2. combination of classical meta learning (learning with structures) and deep learning (learning with huge amounts of dataset with gradients)
3. So what? phase --> deployment in robotics domain

